# ---- Daily markdown output ----
# NOTE: the generated daily review output directory is intentionally NOT
# ignored yet, so the generated markdown can be committed/reviewed for now.
# If output should become throwaway later, add the output dir here
# (e.g. `reviews/` or `output/`).

# ---- slack-daily-review runtime ----
# Local run state: machine-specific, and posted.log is a local audit trail.
state/

# The inbox holds VERBATIM Slack content, including private DMs. Not committed by
# default -- committing it would put colleagues' messages into version control.
# If you want a tracked history of your inbox, delete the line below and commit
# deliberately, knowing what lands in the repo.
INBOX.md
